{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "03492",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 0.6,
      "end_seconds": 5.32,
      "duration_seconds": 4.72,
      "text": "sorry I'm a little late, um, doctor"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 6.74,
      "end_seconds": 10.41,
      "duration_seconds": 3.67,
      "text": "That's fine, sit down. Tell me why you came."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 11.45,
      "end_seconds": 28.06,
      "duration_seconds": 16.61,
      "text": "Sorry, uh, what was I saying, honestly, it's fever and shivers, and my family pushed me to come. I wasn't sure whether to come in at all, to be honest."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 29.31,
      "end_seconds": 32.36,
      "duration_seconds": 3.05,
      "text": "how long has it been like this?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 33.92,
      "end_seconds": 37.07,
      "duration_seconds": 3.15,
      "text": "well, for ten days, I'd say"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 37.65,
      "end_seconds": 40.98,
      "duration_seconds": 3.33,
      "text": "Yes. Is it constant or in episodes?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 45.75,
      "end_seconds": 48.57,
      "duration_seconds": 2.82,
      "text": "It happens every other day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 49.78,
      "end_seconds": 53.6,
      "duration_seconds": 3.82,
      "text": "rate it for me, mild, moderate or severe?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 55.7,
      "end_seconds": 60.52,
      "duration_seconds": 4.82,
      "text": "A seven out of ten, um, I suppose."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 61.2,
      "end_seconds": 64.29,
      "duration_seconds": 3.09,
      "text": "what about confusion, have you noticed that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 66.14,
      "end_seconds": 84.49,
      "duration_seconds": 18.35,
      "text": "Uh, um, yes, for two months. About confusion, I'd call it severe. As for cloudy smelly urine, I honestly can't say when that began. It might have been last month or the month before."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 85.04,
      "end_seconds": 90.1,
      "duration_seconds": 5.06,
      "text": "let me check a few things. Any cough, back pain or fall?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 91.83,
      "end_seconds": 96.68,
      "duration_seconds": 4.85,
      "text": "mm, no, I haven't had any of them"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 98.04,
      "end_seconds": 99.46,
      "duration_seconds": 1.42,
      "text": "What about vomiting?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 101.26,
      "end_seconds": 102.87,
      "duration_seconds": 1.61,
      "text": "Nope, no vomiting."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 107.32,
      "end_seconds": 110.05,
      "duration_seconds": 2.73,
      "text": "Any problems with your joints or muscles?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 112.04,
      "end_seconds": 113.88,
      "duration_seconds": 1.84,
      "text": "no, nothing there"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 120.98,
      "end_seconds": 123.48,
      "duration_seconds": 2.5,
      "text": "Do you have any chronic illnesses?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 128.71,
      "end_seconds": 133.0,
      "duration_seconds": 4.29,
      "text": "I have an irregular heartbeat, for five years."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 133.74,
      "end_seconds": 137.03,
      "duration_seconds": 3.29,
      "text": "Yes. Right, tell me your medicines, please."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 137.62,
      "end_seconds": 146.57,
      "duration_seconds": 8.95,
      "text": "It's warfarin, 3 milligrams, in the evening for the blood thinning. It's a urinary catheter, in place."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 160.64,
      "end_seconds": 162.82,
      "duration_seconds": 2.18,
      "text": "Any surgery in the past?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 167.67,
      "end_seconds": 175.54,
      "duration_seconds": 7.87,
      "text": "Mm, yes, I had a meniscus repair on my knee, four years ago."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 176.76,
      "end_seconds": 179.59,
      "duration_seconds": 2.83,
      "text": "A few questions about your lifestyle now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 180.27,
      "end_seconds": 193.3,
      "duration_seconds": 13.03,
      "text": "I have about eight cigarettes in a day. My husband and I live above the shop. I'm a bus driver, so I sit for long hours."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 194.01,
      "end_seconds": 197.24,
      "duration_seconds": 3.23,
      "text": "Let me ask about allergies, anything at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 198.65,
      "end_seconds": 203.26,
      "duration_seconds": 4.61,
      "text": "Yes, plasters, it gives me a red itchy rash."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 205.22,
      "end_seconds": 207.97,
      "duration_seconds": 2.75,
      "text": "I'll just record a few vital signs"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 221.9,
      "end_seconds": 224.97,
      "duration_seconds": 3.07,
      "text": "Okay, nearly done with the readings..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 237.27,
      "end_seconds": 244.67,
      "duration_seconds": 7.4,
      "text": "Okay: oxygen saturation is 98 percent, blood pressure 107 over 79, pulse is 95 beats a minute."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 246.23,
      "end_seconds": 247.92,
      "duration_seconds": 1.69,
      "text": "Is that okay?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 249.96,
      "end_seconds": 253.56,
      "duration_seconds": 3.6,
      "text": "I'll explain what these mean in a moment."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 255.56,
      "end_seconds": 259.06,
      "duration_seconds": 3.5,
      "text": "now I'm going to do a short physical check"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 260.01,
      "end_seconds": 263.24,
      "duration_seconds": 3.23,
      "text": "Stay as you are for a moment."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 279.75,
      "end_seconds": 286.31,
      "duration_seconds": 6.56,
      "text": "the catheter bag has cloudy urine and there is tenderness above the pubic bone"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 288.56,
      "end_seconds": 291.01,
      "duration_seconds": 2.45,
      "text": "Thank you, you can get dressed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 301.49,
      "end_seconds": 306.64,
      "duration_seconds": 5.15,
      "text": "Taking everything into account, it fits best with a catheter-related urinary infection."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 307.55,
      "end_seconds": 310.24,
      "duration_seconds": 2.69,
      "text": "Actually, is it dangerous, doctor?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 310.88,
      "end_seconds": 341.23,
      "duration_seconds": 30.35,
      "text": "It's reasonable to be concerned, but right now a catheter-related urinary infection is my leading thought, not anything worse. I'd like to arrange a urine culture for possible urinary infection. Let's use co-amoxiclav, 625 milligrams, three times a day, seven days. It's for catheter urinary infection. It's a commonly used medicine and most people tolerate it well. Change the catheter and drink plenty. I'd like you back in two days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 342.91,
      "end_seconds": 347.76,
      "duration_seconds": 4.85,
      "text": "How would you describe the plan, so we're on the same page?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 349.47,
      "end_seconds": 361.61,
      "duration_seconds": 12.14,
      "text": "So, I take the co-amoxiclav, 625 milligrams, three times a day and come back in two days. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 362.48,
      "end_seconds": 366.8,
      "duration_seconds": 4.32,
      "text": "yes, exactly right does all of that make sense?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 367.63,
      "end_seconds": 371.84,
      "duration_seconds": 4.21,
      "text": "right, I'll do that thank you, doctor"
    }
  ]
}